--
N5008 [temp.inst]/2-3: instantiating istream<char> (for the explicit
specialization of its member ignore) instantiates its base ios<...>,
whose typedef num_put<out_iter<char>> leads to out_iter's typedef naming
ostream<char>.  The front end instantiates ostream<char> there, while
ios<...> has only its ios_base members, and ostream<char> keeps that
partial member list: `this->np' in the member template insert is an
"unresolved member expression" and insert's body is dropped (bin53 too).
This is the drop of basic_ostream::_M_insert in libstdc++'s <sstream>
when its `extern template' declarations are disregarded
(cpp11_libstdcxx_header_drops/test_ostream_int; reduced from it).  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
